WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.068 --> 00:00:11.726
The Pop-Song Crew's leadership committee was finishing up their monthly meeting.

2
00:00:11.727 --> 00:00:14.895
The Pop-Song Crew was the school singing club.

3
00:00:14.896 --> 00:00:19.520
"Is there anything else to discuss?" Jerry, the club's president, asked.

4
00:00:19.521 --> 00:00:23.250
"No," Lucy, the treasurer, replied.

5
00:00:23.251 --> 00:00:26.381
Kathy, the secretary, shook her head.

6
00:00:26.382 --> 00:00:30.776
"Yes!" Mrs. Mayer, the club's faculty advisor, said eagerly.

7
00:00:30.777 --> 00:00:33.063
She was looking at her phone.

8
00:00:33.064 --> 00:00:37.709
"We've been invited to sing at the Newtown Spring Festival next month."

9
00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:41.747
The kids cheered.

10
00:00:41.748 --> 00:00:46.148
"I can't wait to tell the rest of the club members," Jerry said.

11
00:00:46.149 --> 00:00:48.373
"Wait," Lucy said.

12
00:00:48.374 --> 00:00:51.125
"Newtown is three hours away.

13
00:00:51.126 --> 00:00:54.023
We'd have to rent a van to get there."

14
00:00:54.024 --> 00:00:58.663
"How much did it cost last time we rented a van?" Mrs. Mayer asked.

15
00:00:58.664 --> 00:01:01.085
Lucy checked the club's account.

16
00:01:01.086 --> 00:01:05.628
"Three hundred dollars. Plus $35 for gas.

17
00:01:05.629 --> 00:01:08.771
We only have twenty dollars left in our account."

18
00:01:08.772 --> 00:01:10.797
She did a quick calculation.

19
00:01:10.798 --> 00:01:14.168
"We'd have to raise $315."

20
00:01:14.169 --> 00:01:17.495
Kathy groaned.

21
00:01:17.496 --> 00:01:21.744
"We can ask everyone in the club to pitch in," Jerry suggested.

22
00:01:21.745 --> 00:01:25.522
Lucy punched the numbers into the calculator app on her phone.

23
00:01:25.523 --> 00:01:31.938
"With 11 members, everyone would have to pay $28.63 each."

24
00:01:31.939 --> 00:01:35.969
"That's a lot for some members," Mrs. Mayer said.

25
00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:40.432
"Especially since we've had many expenses this year."

26
00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:43.946
"We could hold a fundraiser," Kathy suggested.

27
00:01:43.947 --> 00:01:49.104
"Great idea," Jerry said. "How about a car wash?"

28
00:01:49.105 --> 00:01:52.815
"Math Club had one last week," Lucy said.

29
00:01:52.816 --> 00:01:56.112
"A bake sale?" Kathy asked.

30
00:01:56.113 --> 00:02:04.046
"We'd have to sell a lot of cookies to raise $315." Lucy sighed.

31
00:02:04.047 --> 00:02:07.357
"Can we text about this later?" Kathy asked.

32
00:02:07.358 --> 00:02:10.689
"I'm late for a friend's birthday party at the bowling alley."

33
00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:15.378
"Hey! Science Club did a bowling fundraiser last year," Jerry said.

34
00:02:15.379 --> 00:02:17.487
"They raised a lot of money."

35
00:02:17.488 --> 00:02:21.050
"I'll call and find out the costs," Lucy said.

36
00:02:21.051 --> 00:02:23.544
"Then we can figure out a budget."

37
00:02:23.545 --> 00:02:27.145
The next day Lucy sent a group text to the committee.

38
00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:33.325
"Bad news. The bowling alley costs two hundred dollars to rent for two hours.

39
00:02:33.326 --> 00:02:37.666
That means we'd have to raise $515 total."

40
00:02:37.667 --> 00:02:40.575
"Now what?" Jerry texted back.

41
00:02:40.576 --> 00:02:43.534
Lucy sent a shrugging emoticon.

42
00:02:43.535 --> 00:02:46.256
Ten minutes later Kathy texted.

43
00:02:46.257 --> 00:02:48.310
"Can you meet me at the bowling alley?

44
00:02:48.311 --> 00:02:50.708
I think I have a solution!"

45
00:02:50.709 --> 00:02:56.952
When Lucy and Jerry arrived at the bowling alley, Kathy introduced them to her friend Carl.

46
00:02:56.953 --> 00:03:00.224
"I'm a big fan of your club!" Carl said.

47
00:03:00.225 --> 00:03:02.684
"My uncle owns this bowling alley.

48
00:03:02.685 --> 00:03:06.831
He said he'd only charge you one hundred dollars for three hours.

49
00:03:06.832 --> 00:03:09.900
And the rental fee includes the games and shoe rentals.

50
00:03:09.901 --> 00:03:13.446
He thinks this would be great publicity for the bowling alley."

51
00:03:13.447 --> 00:03:18.912
"That means we'd need to raise $415 total," Lucy said.

52
00:03:18.913 --> 00:03:25.393
"If we charge $10 per person, we'll need at least 42 people to come to our fundraiser."

53
00:03:25.394 --> 00:03:30.688
"What if all eleven club members bring three people with them?" Jerry suggested.

54
00:03:30.689 --> 00:03:34.020
"That's 44 people," Kathy said.

55
00:03:34.021 --> 00:03:40.041
"We'd raise $440!" Lucy said. "That's more than enough!"

56
00:03:40.042 --> 00:03:44.203
"This is great, Carl," Jerry said. "Thank you!"

57
00:03:44.204 --> 00:03:49.441
Two weeks later Lucy, Jerry, and Mrs. Mayer sat at a table in the bowling alley.

58
00:03:49.442 --> 00:03:52.103
The fundraiser had been a lot of fun.

59
00:03:52.104 --> 00:03:55.601
Even more people had shown up than they had expected.

60
00:03:55.602 --> 00:03:58.620
"How much did we make?" Kathy asked.

61
00:03:58.621 --> 00:04:00.891
Lucy finished counting the money.

62
00:04:00.892 --> 00:04:04.479
"We made $560.

63
00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:11.106
After we pay $100 to the bowling alley, we have a profit of $460.

64
00:04:11.107 --> 00:04:17.939
That covers the costs of the van and gas, and we'll have $125 left over."

65
00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:21.999
"Plus, the twenty dollars in our account," Mrs. Mayer said.

66
00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:24.818
"We can buy lunch for everyone on the trip."

67
00:04:24.819 --> 00:04:34.128
Jerry smiled. "Thanks to Carl and his uncle, The Pop-Song Crew is going to Newtown!"
